{"reference":"Jeremiah 52","book":"Jeremiah","chapter":52,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Jehoiachin in Babylon","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The closing notice about Jehoiachin describes more than a release from prison: he receives an ongoing daily allowance and eats at the Babylonian king’s table. Administrative tablets from Nebuchadnezzar’s palace record food or oil allocations to a ruler identified as Jehoiachin, king of Judah, along with his dependents and other Judeans. These records provide near-contemporary context for his continued recognition and palace support in Babylon, though they do not independently confirm the particular release scene described here.","verse_refs":["Jeremiah 52:1-34","Jeremiah 52:31-34"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_jeremiah_052_fc8168913666260dc8312124"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"why_it_matters","title":"More Than One Deportation","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"The chapter’s sweep distinguishes Jehoiachin’s earlier removal with selected groups from the later fall of Jerusalem under Zedekiah and the further deportations listed in verses 28–30. Reading these episodes as a sequence helps prevent the Babylonian exile from being treated as one single, undifferentiated departure.","verse_refs":["Jeremiah 52:1-34","Jeremiah 52:31-34"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_jeremiah_052_819ac7fb1f6cf42fa9b8caf7"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Jeremiah’s Closing Chapter","blocks":[{"id":"block_3","text":"Jeremiah is a varied book, bringing together poetry, prose sermons, narratives, letters, headings, restoration collections, oracles against nations, and a concluding appendix. A practical outline places chapter 52 after the nation oracles of chapters 46–51; this arrangement describes the received book without settling how its materials were composed.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_jeremiah_052_38ca6a4d8dacf078e89a4d2f"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}